6.5  Ethernet, MAC addresses and ARP

TL;DR
  - On a local network, frames travel from MAC address to MAC address: 48-bit
    hardware addresses such as f4:92:bf:0e:21:7a.
  - To reach an IP address on the same network, a machine asks "who has this
    IP?" (ARP) and keeps the answer in its neighbour table.
  - A switch learns which MAC address sits behind each port and sends frames
    only there; Wi-Fi does the same through the access point.

      ip neigh          # the neighbour (ARP) table
      ip -br link       # your MAC addresses

On your machine
  L2 link   wlp0s20f3 up · neighbour 192.168.1.1 is f4:92:bf:0e:21:7a on
            wlp0s20f3
  L3 IP     docker0 172.17.0.1/16, wlp0s20f3 192.168.1.23/24, wlp0s20f3
            fe80::8ec6:81ff:fe2a:107f/64 · gateway 192.168.1.1 · forwards
            packets for others
  L4 TCP    12 connections open now; 30,120 started and 410 accepted since boot
            · 1,840 of 3.1 million segments resent
  L4 UDP    95,000 datagrams in, 61,000 out, since boot
  L7 DNS    127.0.0.53

Pitfalls
  - Phones and laptops often use a random MAC address per Wi-Fi network, for
    privacy: a router may list the same device twice.
  - Two machines answering ARP for one address, by mistake or as an attack, make
    connections drop on and off.
  - IPv6 doesn't use ARP: neighbour discovery (NDP) does the same job, with
    ICMPv6.

Deep dive

  ▾ What's in a MAC address?

    Six bytes. The first three often name the manufacturer, the rest the device.
    One bit of the first byte marks "locally administered" addresses, which is
    what random MAC addresses set. ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff is broadcast: every machine
    on the link reads it.

  ▾ Why both MAC and IP addresses?

    IP addresses are logical: they depend on the network you join, and they
    carry a packet across many networks. MAC addresses deliver it on the current
    link, one hop at a time. At each router, the IP addresses stay the same
    while the MAC addresses change.

Related
  Commands  ip
  Paths     /proc/net/arp
  Hub       atfq network Network
